0.4 Bibliographic metadata
A document’s identity is written once, in biblio.xml, and then derived everywhere else. The file conforms to biblio.dtd in pdai/pipeline/ai-scholar/src/ai_scholar/schemas/. Required fields are entrytype, biblabel, at least one author, title, and year. Everything else is optional and is omitted when the printed source does not give it.






WarningNever invent a bibliographic field



Every value in biblio.xml is read off the title page or the imprint / CIP page of that volume. A field the book does not print stays absent. Band I of Bischoff does not name an editor on the title page, so Bischoff1998 has no &lt;editor&gt; — even though Bands II and III name Birgit Ebersperger.



Band II, taken from the title page (PDF p.001) and the imprint (PDF p.002).
&lt;biblio&gt;
  &lt;entrytype&gt;book&lt;/entrytype&gt;
  &lt;biblabel&gt;Bischoff2004&lt;/biblabel&gt;
  &lt;author&gt;Bischoff, Bernhard&lt;/author&gt;
  &lt;editor&gt;Ebersperger, Birgit&lt;/editor&gt;
  &lt;title&gt;Katalog der festländischen Handschriften des
         neunten Jahrhunderts (mit Ausnahme der wisigotischen)&lt;/title&gt;
  &lt;subtitle&gt;Teil II: LAON – PADERBORN&lt;/subtitle&gt;
  &lt;series&gt;Veröffentlichungen der Kommission für die Herausgabe
          der mittelalterlichen Bibliothekskataloge
          Deutschlands und der Schweiz&lt;/series&gt;
  &lt;year&gt;2004&lt;/year&gt;
  &lt;publisher&gt;Harrassowitz Verlag&lt;/publisher&gt;
  &lt;address&gt;Wiesbaden&lt;/address&gt;
  &lt;isbn&gt;3-447-04750-X&lt;/isbn&gt;
  &lt;language&gt;de&lt;/language&gt;
&lt;/biblio&gt;
biblabel matches the folder name. The half-title of this volume prints the Bayerische Akademie der Wissenschaften as the issuing body of the series, not as the author — so the academy is not in &lt;author&gt;.

bibliography.yaml in the collection (and, for the code tree, in pdai/collections/&lt;name&gt;/config/) is the working record of those verified fields, with a _provenance note naming the printed page. It is the file a setup script reads when it writes biblio.xml. It is not a second bibliography and it is not cited.
The collection file &lt;name&gt;.bib is generated:
python -m ai_lemma_index.stanzadoc.bib_build --collection medieval-sec
bib_build walks every document folder, reads biblio.xml, and writes one BibLaTeX entry whose key is the folder name. Documents without biblio.xml get no entry — a gap, not a guessed record. Hand-editing the .bib is overwritten the next time the command runs.
pdai-config.json is a different kind of metadata. It records how the document was harvested and processed: source PDF path, page count, OCR model, collection name, and — once the schema exists — a schema_ref pointing at the DTDs on the collection. It is not the bibliography. Correcting a title means editing biblio.xml and rebuilding the bib, then updating the document block in pdai-config.json so the two do not drift.

2.3 The prompt composer
The OCR prompt of every collection is built by one function, ocr_runner.cure_config.compose(collection, model, volume=…). Its layers, in fixed order:

page language — agents/infrastructure/ai-instructions/ocr/pdai-page-language.j2, rendered with the vocabulary of the collection’s grammar (marker and note types, extension types, forbidden aliases);
base — collections/&lt;c&gt;/ai-instructions/&lt;prefix&gt;.base.j2;
volume — &lt;prefix&gt;.&lt;volume&gt;.j2, optional;
engine — &lt;prefix&gt;.&lt;engine&gt;.j2, optional; engine notes only;
volume.engine — &lt;prefix&gt;.&lt;volume&gt;.&lt;engine&gt;.j2, optional.

The base holds the Jinja slots page_language and engine_notes; it also receives page_grammar, the admitted content of every element read from the DTD, for bases that list what may stand inside what. The engine key of a model comes from the one table at the top of collections/ocr_catalog.yaml (qwen3.8 → qwen38, qwen3-vl → qwen3vl, kimi → kimi, gemini-3.8 → gemini38). The instruction family of a collection is named in its cure.yaml or, without one, in its catalog entry.
Instruction families live in the collection folder beside config/. The central store keeps only the universal fragment and generic templates (archival-letter-page.j2, full_page_scholarly.j2 …). Superseded versions are kept in ai-instructions/versions/&lt;engine&gt;/. ai-scholar’s own templates, which it renders without includes, carry the fragment as a generated block kept in step by python -m ocr_runner.page_language sync-ai-scholar (--check fails when a block has drifted).

