17.1.1 Gate

the validity fail count of the scope is not higher than in the diagnosis;
the structural defect count is not higher;
no code appears that the diagnosis did not report;
one repaired page is inspected on the viewer port, facsimile next to the rendering, before the iteration is reported as done.

The op pdai:cure_certify compares the counts of the diagnosis with the new counts and fails on a new class or a higher count.

17.2 Stage 7 — Downstream
~/ai-mac-studio/pdai/index/ai-lemma-index/.venv/bin/pdai-complete --collection &lt;c&gt; --dry-run
~/ai-mac-studio/pdai/index/ai-lemma-index/.venv/bin/pdai-complete --collection &lt;c&gt;
~/ai-mac-studio/pdai/index/ai-lemma-index/.venv/bin/pdai-corpus-audit --collection &lt;c&gt;
pdai-complete runs stanza → corpus → lemma → gazetteer → chroma, with a corpus audit at start and end. It does not run OCR or structure.xml; those gaps are reported. Changed pages are detected by the content hash text_sha256 of the page, not by the file modification time; a normalizer that only rewrites attributes therefore does not make a page stale.






NoteCommand names



The corpus audit is pdai-corpus-audit (package ai-lemma-index). The name pdai-audit belongs to the structural audit of pipeline/schema-audit. Both packages used to define pdai-audit; whichever was installed last shadowed the other.



17.2.1 Gate

status.json reports search_ready, or names the gaps;
the language gate passes: no language with at least 100 sentences before the run loses more than 5 % of them, unless the run is given --allow-lang-drop on purpose;
a Glider query (port 5890) returns a hit from a repaired page.

The language gate exists because of an observed failure: a Stanza cache without the Latin and French models dropped those sentences and still reported every page as processed (see the Copernicus case).
